From 18a5dab0ed660b31363e5e1bbf9f6dd1ac713f07 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ss3ds <ss3ds@localhost>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 02:59:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ss3ds: hook 0162 fix 0123 field Pokemon menu context name
 (FIELD -> _0)

Hook 0123's inserted code referenced PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_FIELD, which
does not exist in the staged decomp, so it failed to compile and the
0159 build guard then stopped the build even though hook 0124 repaired
the name afterwards. Hook 0124 already established that the field
Pokemon menu context is PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_0 (launch_application.c
PartyMenu_LaunchApp_Unk1) and proved it compiles. Make 0123 emit the
correct name from the start, so it applies first try and 0124 becomes
a no-op. The built game code is unchanged versus the 0124 repair.
---
 scripts/ss3ds_hooks.d/0123_pmshortcuts.py | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/ss3ds_hooks.d/0123_pmshortcuts.py b/scripts/ss3ds_hooks.d/0123_pmshortcuts.py
index 8a490a7..6b4f588 100644
--- a/scripts/ss3ds_hooks.d/0123_pmshortcuts.py
+++ b/scripts/ss3ds_hooks.d/0123_pmshortcuts.py
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 #!/usr/bin/env python3
 """ss3ds 0123: Pokemon-menu shortcuts (Settings > Play "Pokemon menu X / Y", default OFF). Applied to the staged decomp in cwd (= $C).
-  party_menu.c  PartyMenu_Subtask_MainNormal: in the field's Pokemon menu (PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_FIELD) with a Pokemon highlighted,
+  party_menu.c  PartyMenu_Subtask_MainNormal: in the field's Pokemon menu (PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_0) with a Pokemon highlighted,
                 X = Move Reminder, Y = Move Tutor. Both exit the menu with a port-only action code (0xA0 / 0xA1).
                 Move Reminder opens only when the Pokemon has a level-up move it forgot (the NPC's own list); the tutor offers the
                 one move HGSS's Blackthorn tutors would offer that Pokemon (Draco Meteor for Dragon types, Blast Burn / Hydro Cannon /
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ static int SS3DS_PartyQol(PartyMenu *partyMenu) {
     u16 *eligible;
     u16 move;
     int ok;
-    if (partyMenu->args->context != PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_FIELD || !P3DS_PmShortcutsCfg()) {
+    if (partyMenu->args->context != PARTY_MENU_CONTEXT_0 || !P3DS_PmShortcutsCfg()) {
         return 0;
     }
     if (!sHinted) {
-- 
